{
  "name": "invite-payload-encoding",
  "description": "Invite link fragment payload (https://<host>/j#v1.<base64url(this)>) as canonical CBOR: [server, invite mailbox, invite secret, inviter fingerprint, expires, gateway pins (array of 1 to 4 SHA-256 key config hashes of the server's OHTTP gateway), push relay pins (array of 0 to 4 hashes of its push relay's key config), map host pins (array of 0 to 4 hashes of the key config of the map host its server forwards relayed downloads to), registration code (text; present only when the inviter passes one on, so the array has 8 elements without it and 9 with it)] (design D, invite flow; join flow A: nothing about the Party, and no use count, since every invite waits for the inviter and stops after the first joiner is let in; design B.1 registration codes; B.12 key pinning: a joiner new to the server pins the inviter's hashes, never the first key it sees). An empty registration code is refused.",
